1
00:00:15,203 --> 00:00:17,371
HA JUNG-WOO

2
00:00:17,372 --> 00:00:19,374
IM SOO-JUNG

3
00:00:22,753 --> 00:00:25,005
KIM JUN-HAN

4
00:00:25,422 --> 00:00:27,257
KRYSTAL JUNG

5
00:00:33,513 --> 00:00:35,641
SHIM EUN-KYUNG

6
00:00:54,368 --> 00:00:59,039
MAD CONCRETE DREAMS

7
00:01:02,250 --> 00:01:04,753
NINE YEARS AGO

8
00:01:05,420 --> 00:01:07,339
I'm not into this stuff.

9
00:01:08,340 --> 00:01:10,257
Yi-gyeong, can't you go in alone?

10
00:01:10,258 --> 00:01:11,592
Come on, Seon.

11
00:01:11,593 --> 00:01:14,680
Is there anyone in Korea who's successful
that doesn't believe in fortunes?

12
00:01:15,138 --> 00:01:17,974
My mom trusts Ms. Park
more than what lawyers say.

13
00:01:18,684 --> 00:01:20,519
She says Ms. Park made her rich.

14
00:01:21,019 --> 00:01:22,312
- Rich?
- Yes.

15
00:01:22,521 --> 00:01:25,773
So just close your eyes
and give it a try, okay?

16
00:01:25,774 --> 00:01:28,734
Who knows?
Maybe a big fortune will show up, right?

17
00:01:28,735 --> 00:01:31,529
But I still don't want to.
It feels wasteful.

18
00:01:31,530 --> 00:01:32,280
Wasteful?

19
00:01:32,572 --> 00:01:34,740
If you go with me, it's a free pass.

20
00:01:34,741 --> 00:01:37,702
I mean, it's just that
I always come with my mom.

21
00:01:37,703 --> 00:01:40,997
This is the first time I'm coming alone,
so I'm a bit anxious, okay?

22
00:01:41,498 --> 00:01:44,042
I really have no one else to ask
besides you.

23
00:01:45,252 --> 00:01:46,044
Fine.

24
00:01:47,029 --> 00:01:49,976
MS. PARK

25
00:01:52,634 --> 00:01:53,677
What's your relationship?

26
00:01:54,636 --> 00:01:55,803
She's a close friend.

27
00:01:55,804 --> 00:01:56,513
Why?

28
00:01:56,722 --> 00:01:57,722
Hmm...

29
00:01:57,723 --> 00:01:59,141
Sharp and decisive.

30
00:02:01,184 --> 00:02:04,229
The whole house is going dark
like it's struck by lightning.

31
00:02:06,148 --> 00:02:08,400
What does that mean?

32
00:02:08,817 --> 00:02:11,194
You won't listen to me anyway,
so why did you come back?

33
00:02:11,778 --> 00:02:12,653
You.

34
00:02:12,654 --> 00:02:14,489
I told you not to marry that guy, right?

35
00:02:14,906 --> 00:02:17,575
But you said
there was a way out.

36
00:02:17,576 --> 00:02:18,910
The marriage is already done.

37
00:02:19,578 --> 00:02:21,246
The only way to survive

38
00:02:21,747 --> 00:02:22,998
is through the child.

39
00:02:23,248 --> 00:02:25,083
But is that easy?

40
00:02:25,667 --> 00:02:27,543
Even a flickering light

41
00:02:27,544 --> 00:02:29,546
is fragile in the breeze.

42
00:02:30,338 --> 00:02:31,339
What do you mean?

43
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:33,674
No need to say things
that don't make sense.

44
00:02:33,675 --> 00:02:35,342
Just tell me how.

45
00:02:35,343 --> 00:02:36,510
At least use a talisman.

46
00:02:36,511 --> 00:02:38,596
Even the great former lady

47
00:02:38,597 --> 00:02:40,182
can't beat her daughter.

48
00:02:40,474 --> 00:02:42,725
What can I say to you, girl?

49
00:02:42,726 --> 00:02:45,352
Anyway, you only pick up
what you want to hear!

50
00:02:45,353 --> 00:02:47,396
Why do you
keep on calling me a girl?

51
00:02:47,397 --> 00:02:49,106
I can't believe this.

52
00:02:49,107 --> 00:02:50,983
You really talk so rudely!

53
00:02:50,984 --> 00:02:52,194
- I mean...
- Yi-gyeong.

54
00:02:53,320 --> 00:02:56,071
But she's being so rude.

55
00:02:56,072 --> 00:02:57,449
Am I overreacting, Seon?

56
00:02:57,783 --> 00:03:00,159
Hey, let's just go.

57
00:03:00,160 --> 00:03:02,662
I guess you need to hear me.

58
00:03:03,538 --> 00:03:04,206
Pardon?

59
00:03:04,539 --> 00:03:06,958
Your husband
splurged recently, right?

60
00:03:07,793 --> 00:03:08,752
What is this?

61
00:03:09,419 --> 00:03:10,212
A building?

62
00:03:13,131 --> 00:03:15,550
I hear it, I hear it...

63
00:03:17,260 --> 00:03:19,387
I hear it...

64
00:03:25,560 --> 00:03:26,561
Handcuffs.

65
00:03:27,062 --> 00:03:28,104
Prison uniform.

66
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:29,856
Handcuffs?

67
00:03:31,525 --> 00:03:32,942
If you just leave him,

68
00:03:32,943 --> 00:03:34,110
your husband will go to prison.

69
00:03:37,781 --> 00:03:40,700
Well, that person is someone
who can live without the law.

70
00:03:41,743 --> 00:03:42,869
Do you want to go with him?

71
00:03:44,579 --> 00:03:45,329
What?

72
00:03:45,330 --> 00:03:46,498
If you don't want to go together...

73
00:03:47,624 --> 00:03:48,708
Use a talisman.

74
00:03:49,835 --> 00:03:50,710
Gosh...

75
00:03:51,711 --> 00:03:52,419
I'm leaving.

76
00:03:52,420 --> 00:03:53,672
Your child is sick, right?

77
00:03:55,924 --> 00:03:57,341
You two

78
00:03:57,342 --> 00:04:00,220
shouldn't have met as a couple,
but here we are.

79
00:04:02,973 --> 00:04:05,642
Let's see.

80
00:04:08,353 --> 00:04:09,145
Huh?

81
00:04:12,732 --> 00:04:14,401
It's a prayer bead made from a meteorite.

82
00:04:15,068 --> 00:04:16,444
Make sure to carry it with you.

83
00:04:17,404 --> 00:04:20,072
Your kid will do great,

84
00:04:20,073 --> 00:04:21,533
and your husband will be safe too.

85
00:04:22,576 --> 00:04:23,410
Take it!

86
00:04:24,077 --> 00:04:25,912
Yes.

87
00:04:27,789 --> 00:04:28,748
One million won.

88
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:30,709
What?

89
00:04:30,876 --> 00:04:32,711
It's your first time,
so I gave you a big discount.

90
00:04:40,343 --> 00:04:41,511
Listen carefully.

91
00:04:43,346 --> 00:04:45,974
MAD CONCRETE DREAMS

92
00:04:50,729 --> 00:04:51,855
Mr. Gi?

93
00:04:52,022 --> 00:04:53,982
EPISODE 8
Hey, what are you doing right now?

94
00:04:54,691 --> 00:04:57,026
You can't drink beer
at convenience stores these days.

95
00:04:57,027 --> 00:04:58,111
Oh, really?

96
00:05:00,572 --> 00:05:03,157
We have some good liquor
at our real estate office.

97
00:05:03,158 --> 00:05:03,909
Let's go.

98
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:25,512
I saved this drink
for a special guest.

99
00:05:25,513 --> 00:05:27,807
- I got it from Kyoto.
- Wow.

100
00:05:31,144 --> 00:05:32,145
Okay.

101
00:05:34,940 --> 00:05:35,899
Wow.

102
00:05:40,403 --> 00:05:41,279
Yes.

103
00:05:47,953 --> 00:05:49,079
Whoa!

104
00:05:50,789 --> 00:05:53,666
Hey, what's wrong, Hee-ju?

105
00:05:53,667 --> 00:05:55,250
Oh, I'm sorry.

106
00:05:55,251 --> 00:05:56,752
I suddenly have a fever.

107
00:05:56,753 --> 00:05:58,254
Oh.

108
00:06:02,509 --> 00:06:05,017
Goodness.

109
00:06:13,103 --> 00:06:14,145
Hey, boss.

110
00:06:15,397 --> 00:06:16,773
About Mr. Nam.

111
00:06:17,983 --> 00:06:19,484
Don't trust that guy too much.

112
00:06:20,360 --> 00:06:22,946
That money-grubbing scumbag.

113
00:06:23,446 --> 00:06:25,448
Seriously, he's obsessed with money.

114
00:06:29,411 --> 00:06:30,328
Why?

115
00:06:33,915 --> 00:06:35,666
What is it? Something wrong?

116
00:06:35,667 --> 00:06:37,668
Boss, you're the same.

117
00:06:37,669 --> 00:06:38,545
What about me?

118
00:06:40,964 --> 00:06:43,008
You said you would give me shares.

119
00:06:43,925 --> 00:06:45,467
You promised me a bonus

120
00:06:45,468 --> 00:06:47,219
when you took over Han-maum.

121
00:06:47,220 --> 00:06:48,303
Congratulations!

122
00:06:48,304 --> 00:06:49,930
You really hit the jackpot at 30 billion!

123
00:06:49,931 --> 00:06:51,515
This is all thanks to you, Hee-ju.

124
00:06:51,516 --> 00:06:53,684
So, am I getting a bonus?

125
00:06:53,685 --> 00:06:55,186
Oh, absolutely.
Let's talk about it outside.

126
00:06:56,688 --> 00:07:00,315
Oh, right! I missed the timing.

127
00:07:00,316 --> 00:07:01,693
My goodness.

128
00:07:01,985 --> 00:07:03,736
- Okay, I'll take care of it.
- Oh.

129
00:07:03,737 --> 00:07:04,779
I was thinking about it.

130
00:07:05,363 --> 00:07:06,114
Really?

131
00:07:06,364 --> 00:07:08,741
Here. This is a gift card.

132
00:07:08,742 --> 00:07:11,535
There are many partner stores,

133
00:07:11,536 --> 00:07:12,829
so it'll be easy to use.

134
00:07:13,371 --> 00:07:14,497
Seriously?

135
00:07:17,709 --> 00:07:20,837
- Well, cheers then.
- Oh, sure

136
00:07:21,337 --> 00:07:22,839
- Have more.
- Oh my.

137
00:07:23,673 --> 00:07:25,008
You can pour slowly.

138
00:07:25,925 --> 00:07:27,760
To reconstruction.

139
00:07:27,761 --> 00:07:30,804
Let's make it fun and productive

140
00:07:30,805 --> 00:07:32,056
and live with blessings.

141
00:07:32,057 --> 00:07:32,766
Okay!

142
00:07:41,399 --> 00:07:42,400
Hee-ju,

143
00:07:43,860 --> 00:07:44,986
do you know about love?

144
00:07:45,904 --> 00:07:46,863
Huh?

145
00:07:50,200 --> 00:07:51,366
What is it?

146
00:07:51,367 --> 00:07:53,787
Something must have
happened with your lady.

147
00:07:55,038 --> 00:07:56,081
No.

148
00:07:58,541 --> 00:07:59,666
What's going on?

149
00:07:59,667 --> 00:08:01,419
You know I have good intuition, right?

150
00:08:01,920 --> 00:08:03,922
Just looking at you,
I can tell something's up.

151
00:08:04,380 --> 00:08:05,465
No.

152
00:08:06,883 --> 00:08:08,093
Maybe it's an affair?

153
00:08:11,721 --> 00:08:12,806
Affair?

154
00:08:15,016 --> 00:08:19,604
♪ The wind, the wind,
the wind is blowing ♪

155
00:08:20,772 --> 00:08:23,608
- ♪ The wind is blowing... ♪
- Oh, right. The wind.

156
00:08:24,442 --> 00:08:25,526
Who is it?

157
00:08:25,527 --> 00:08:27,612
Is it you or your lady?

158
00:08:28,530 --> 00:08:29,447
Hee-ju.

159
00:08:30,907 --> 00:08:31,950
Listen to me for a second.

160
00:08:32,283 --> 00:08:34,202
Legally, when getting a divorce,

161
00:08:35,036 --> 00:08:37,371
the one who cheated is at fault, right?

162
00:08:37,372 --> 00:08:38,997
That means when dividing assets,

163
00:08:38,998 --> 00:08:40,666
it's advantageous for the person
who didn't cheat.

164
00:08:40,667 --> 00:08:42,334
- Yes.
- The person who didn't cheat.

165
00:08:42,335 --> 00:08:44,211
I didn't cheat.

166
00:08:44,212 --> 00:08:46,548
But Seon did cheat.

167
00:08:47,257 --> 00:08:48,800
Really? With who?

168
00:08:50,718 --> 00:08:51,760
I can't tell you.

169
00:08:51,761 --> 00:08:55,640
Oh no.

170
00:08:57,934 --> 00:09:00,562
Gosh, I'm the one
who got cheated on.

171
00:09:01,437 --> 00:09:03,439
Why do I feel so disadvantaged?

172
00:09:04,107 --> 00:09:05,065
No.

173
00:09:05,066 --> 00:09:05,899
No way.

174
00:09:05,900 --> 00:09:07,819
Our boss is not at a disadvantage.

175
00:09:08,278 --> 00:09:11,030
Our boss hasn't done
anything wrong, right?

176
00:09:11,573 --> 00:09:14,533
Just file for divorce already.

177
00:09:14,534 --> 00:09:18,120
That way, whether it's custody
or asset division,

178
00:09:18,121 --> 00:09:20,707
it'll all be in your favor.

179
00:09:22,333 --> 00:09:24,794
Hee-ju, you seem to know
one thing but not the other.

180
00:09:28,131 --> 00:09:29,799
Love is absolute power.

181
00:09:30,884 --> 00:09:33,303
Love is way above the law.

182
00:09:34,971 --> 00:09:37,640
So the one who loves more
is always at a disadvantage.

183
00:09:39,517 --> 00:09:41,268
I...

184
00:09:41,269 --> 00:09:43,437
I love Seon more.

185
00:09:43,438 --> 00:09:45,397
- Oh.
- I'm such a fool.

186
00:09:45,398 --> 00:09:47,066
I feel so bad.

187
00:09:49,235 --> 00:09:51,529
Seriously.

188
00:09:53,364 --> 00:09:55,532
It must be
so hard for you, boss.

189
00:09:55,533 --> 00:10:03,374
- ♪ Wind, oh wind ♪
- Oh, what do I do?

190
00:10:04,083 --> 00:10:08,755
♪ Wind ♪

191
00:10:09,672 --> 00:10:12,050
Wind...

192
00:10:36,991 --> 00:10:38,243
It looks good.

193
00:10:42,997 --> 00:10:45,040
I want to file a report
on Jeon Yi-gyeong,

194
00:10:45,041 --> 00:10:47,126
the heiress of Pyeong-buk Gwan,
for domestic violence.

195
00:10:51,923 --> 00:10:53,132
Boss.

196
00:10:57,011 --> 00:10:58,972
- Boss.
- Huh?

197
00:11:18,074 --> 00:11:19,200
Boss.

198
00:11:23,871 --> 00:11:27,292
MIN HWAL-SUNG

199
00:11:29,794 --> 00:11:33,756
Boss, I have some major info.
Want to make a deal?

200
00:11:38,011 --> 00:11:39,803
Being married for 10 years,

201
00:11:39,804 --> 00:11:43,432
I've endured relentless violence,
verbal abuse,

202
00:11:43,433 --> 00:11:46,102
and all kinds of humiliation.

203
00:11:51,107 --> 00:11:51,899
What is this?

204
00:11:53,026 --> 00:11:57,487
Boss, I have some major info.
Want to make a deal?

205
00:11:57,488 --> 00:11:58,239
Gosh.

206
00:11:59,949 --> 00:12:02,285
Does she only text
when she needs something?

207
00:12:05,413 --> 00:12:06,497
What's this guy doing?

208
00:12:13,588 --> 00:12:16,089
Hee-ju

209
00:12:16,090 --> 00:12:17,216
Do you know about love?

210
00:12:18,968 --> 00:12:20,177
What is it?

211
00:12:20,178 --> 00:12:22,555
Something must have
happened with your lady.

212
00:12:49,791 --> 00:12:51,000
Gosh.

213
00:12:52,168 --> 00:12:53,920
I can tell something's going on.

214
00:12:54,128 --> 00:12:57,590
♪ This wind... ♪

215
00:12:58,758 --> 00:13:01,594
- ♪ Wind ♪
- ♪ Wind ♪

216
00:13:10,561 --> 00:13:11,396
Hee-ju.

217
00:13:22,740 --> 00:13:23,574
Hee-ju?

218
00:13:24,784 --> 00:13:25,618
Hee-ju.

219
00:13:32,375 --> 00:13:33,334
Hee-ju.

220
00:13:34,127 --> 00:13:35,711
What time is it?

221
00:13:39,090 --> 00:13:40,049
Hee-ju.

222
00:13:41,092 --> 00:13:41,968
Wake up.

223
00:13:43,469 --> 00:13:44,470
Hee-ju...

224
00:14:06,367 --> 00:14:07,160
Get in.

225
00:14:25,803 --> 00:14:27,430
What's wrong? Why so tense?

226
00:14:28,639 --> 00:14:30,016
I liked you from the start.

227
00:14:31,017 --> 00:14:31,809
What did you say?

228
00:14:35,021 --> 00:14:38,107
I liked you since the day
Su-jong first brought you around.

229
00:14:39,108 --> 00:14:41,444
I hoped you two would break up so badly.

230
00:14:41,861 --> 00:14:43,488
Stop it.

231
00:14:44,697 --> 00:14:46,282
That was a mistake, you know?

232
00:14:46,616 --> 00:14:48,618
Before you two got married,

233
00:14:49,076 --> 00:14:50,786
if I confessed
my feelings back then,

234
00:14:52,455 --> 00:14:53,915
would we have gotten married?

235
00:14:54,707 --> 00:14:55,583
I'm leaving.

236
00:14:57,835 --> 00:15:00,003
Legally, when getting a divorce,

237
00:15:00,004 --> 00:15:02,255
The one who cheated is at fault, right?

238
00:15:02,256 --> 00:15:04,633
That means when dividing assets,
it's advantageous for the person

239
00:15:04,634 --> 00:15:07,010
- What's this?
- who didn't cheat.

240
00:15:07,011 --> 00:15:08,888
Su-jong is preparing to divorce you.

241
00:15:09,305 --> 00:15:11,348
But Seon did cheat.

242
00:15:11,349 --> 00:15:11,933
What?

243
00:15:12,475 --> 00:15:14,101
You're going to get blindsided.

244
00:15:16,437 --> 00:15:19,272
Oh no.

245
00:15:19,273 --> 00:15:21,526
That's Hee-ju from real estate, right?

246
00:15:25,154 --> 00:15:26,614
Just sitting around,
you'll become the sucker.

247
00:15:27,740 --> 00:15:29,158
You need to prepare for divorce too.

248
00:15:30,576 --> 00:15:32,453
Su-jong has committed some crimes.

249
00:15:33,371 --> 00:15:34,955
Kidnapping Yi-gyeong,

250
00:15:34,956 --> 00:15:36,831
plus Oh Dong-ki

251
00:15:36,832 --> 00:15:38,000
and my mother-in-law's murder.

252
00:15:38,751 --> 00:15:40,628
We need to get a solid grip on this.

253
00:15:42,421 --> 00:15:43,339
I'll help you.

254
00:15:51,556 --> 00:15:52,682
What are you doing?

255
00:15:55,977 --> 00:15:57,728
We all know each other,

256
00:15:58,271 --> 00:15:59,188
inside and out.

257
00:16:00,189 --> 00:16:01,941
What is this? Let go!

258
00:16:03,359 --> 00:16:04,986
It's okay.

259
00:16:05,987 --> 00:16:07,655
If not me, who else is going to help you?

260
00:16:08,573 --> 00:16:10,408
- Cut it out.
- Come here!

261
00:16:10,866 --> 00:16:12,201
I said let go!

262
00:16:12,743 --> 00:16:15,036
My nose!

263
00:16:15,037 --> 00:16:16,414
I need to ask directly.

264
00:16:17,331 --> 00:16:18,832
Hey, Seon, listen to me...

265
00:16:18,833 --> 00:16:20,209
You need to listen to me, Seon!

266
00:16:23,838 --> 00:16:27,466
From this moment, we need to prepare
for divorce and gather everything we can!

267
00:16:29,719 --> 00:16:33,639
The proposal for a partnership
is still valid, so think it over.

268
00:16:36,183 --> 00:16:37,768
SEON

269
00:16:38,936 --> 00:16:40,646
- Seon?
- Hello?

270
00:16:41,939 --> 00:16:43,106
Who are you with right now?

271
00:16:43,107 --> 00:16:45,025
Just a second.

272
00:16:45,026 --> 00:16:46,611
Can you come this way?

273
00:16:47,153 --> 00:16:48,613
Let's talk face-to-face for a bit.

274
00:16:49,238 --> 00:16:50,281
Where are you now?

275
00:16:51,574 --> 00:16:52,908
I'm at Hee-ju's real estate office.

276
00:16:53,451 --> 00:16:54,535
Okay, wait for me.

277
00:16:55,536 --> 00:16:56,078
Okay.

278
00:17:13,137 --> 00:17:13,971
Honey.

279
00:17:22,396 --> 00:17:23,314
She's dead.

280
00:17:25,274 --> 00:17:26,316
Did you kill her?

281
00:17:26,317 --> 00:17:27,401
You think I'm that crazy?

282
00:17:45,336 --> 00:17:46,545
Damn it.

283
00:17:52,134 --> 00:17:54,470
I woke up and she was dead.

284
00:17:54,970 --> 00:17:57,264
I really didn't do anything, I swear.

285
00:17:59,642 --> 00:18:01,101
But seriously,

286
00:18:01,102 --> 00:18:02,269
what's this about dividing assets?

287
00:18:03,104 --> 00:18:05,106
Did you tell Hee-ju you wanted a divorce?

288
00:18:05,898 --> 00:18:06,982
How did you find that out?

289
00:18:07,858 --> 00:18:09,151
Min Hwal-sung told me.

290
00:18:10,695 --> 00:18:11,987
How did that jerk know?

291
00:18:12,196 --> 00:18:14,740
He played me a recording of your voice.

292
00:18:19,870 --> 00:18:21,080
What about my share?

293
00:18:22,498 --> 00:18:23,540
Your share?

294
00:18:23,541 --> 00:18:24,375
What's that about?

295
00:18:25,209 --> 00:18:27,001
We agreed to split it.

296
00:18:27,002 --> 00:18:29,504
Hey, that's because you called
the cops and messed it up.

297
00:18:29,505 --> 00:18:30,714
I told you, right?

298
00:18:30,715 --> 00:18:32,966
I didn't call the police.
My mother-in-law did.

299
00:18:32,967 --> 00:18:34,635
Oh, this guy is trying to be slick again.

300
00:18:35,761 --> 00:18:37,221
This was all Hwal-sung's idea.

301
00:18:37,722 --> 00:18:38,514
What do you mean?

302
00:18:39,181 --> 00:18:40,223
Wait.

303
00:18:40,224 --> 00:18:41,851
A while ago,

304
00:18:42,435 --> 00:18:44,894
he came to me asking for shares
in the Seyoon Building.

305
00:18:44,895 --> 00:18:46,438
He caused a huge scene about it.

306
00:18:46,439 --> 00:18:47,690
But I refused.

307
00:18:48,607 --> 00:18:51,484
So he plotted to divide us

308
00:18:51,485 --> 00:18:53,153
to take over Seyoon Building.

309
00:18:53,154 --> 00:18:54,363
That's the plan he devised.

310
00:18:56,073 --> 00:18:58,032
How is that

311
00:18:58,033 --> 00:19:00,243
related to Hee-ju's death?

312
00:19:00,244 --> 00:19:02,913
Do you think Hee-ju would
just hand over that recording for free?

313
00:19:03,831 --> 00:19:06,374
While passing that to him,
he must have made

314
00:19:06,375 --> 00:19:08,794
some demands and it led to a fight.

315
00:19:09,253 --> 00:19:12,172
So, while I was asleep, they were talking
about the recording and shares

316
00:19:12,173 --> 00:19:13,174
and this mess happened.

317
00:19:15,217 --> 00:19:17,511
This is such a mess.

318
00:19:17,887 --> 00:19:19,137
I mean, still,

319
00:19:19,138 --> 00:19:20,764
would Hwal-sung kill someone?

320
00:19:20,765 --> 00:19:21,932
You don't know that guy?

321
00:19:22,808 --> 00:19:24,768
Don't you remember
Hwal-sung was the kidnapper?

322
00:19:24,769 --> 00:19:26,604
I'm divorcing Yi-gyeong.

323
00:19:27,563 --> 00:19:28,981
Both of us will divorce

324
00:19:30,608 --> 00:19:32,776
and take the redevelopment project

325
00:19:32,777 --> 00:19:33,986
for ourselves.

326
00:19:35,070 --> 00:19:37,113
If we plan the operation well,

327
00:19:37,114 --> 00:19:38,240
we can pull it off.

328
00:19:40,409 --> 00:19:43,244
That guy is willing
to strangle me

329
00:19:43,245 --> 00:19:45,539
if he just gets his share.

330
00:19:48,167 --> 00:19:50,252
But where is Hee-ju's phone?

331
00:19:54,840 --> 00:19:55,965
What are you doing?

332
00:19:55,966 --> 00:19:59,261
The phone
should have the call history.

333
00:20:03,265 --> 00:20:04,099
Honey, come here.

334
00:20:05,017 --> 00:20:05,850
Excuse me!

335
00:20:05,851 --> 00:20:06,685
Is anyone here?

336
00:20:11,357 --> 00:20:12,399
Jeez.

337
00:20:16,320 --> 00:20:16,904
Hold on.

338
00:20:21,325 --> 00:20:23,035
What's going on?

339
00:20:32,419 --> 00:20:33,170
Did they leave?

340
00:20:34,713 --> 00:20:35,505
Yes.

341
00:20:35,506 --> 00:20:36,423
Did they really leave?

342
00:20:36,799 --> 00:20:37,758
Yes, they left.

343
00:20:40,761 --> 00:20:42,096
Honey.

344
00:20:44,515 --> 00:20:45,432
You believe me, right?

345
00:20:48,102 --> 00:20:49,061
What?

346
00:20:49,687 --> 00:20:50,771
You don't trust me?

347
00:20:52,940 --> 00:20:54,316
When you're drunk,

348
00:20:55,234 --> 00:20:56,694
you're oblivious to everything
and just fall asleep.

349
00:20:56,944 --> 00:20:57,653
Yes.

350
00:20:58,320 --> 00:20:59,613
Seriously,

351
00:21:01,240 --> 00:21:03,075
after I fell asleep,
I don't remember anything.

352
00:21:09,415 --> 00:21:10,249
Huh?

353
00:21:15,588 --> 00:21:17,673
- Huh?
- What is it?

354
00:21:18,048 --> 00:21:20,466
Ms. Kim Seon, where are you?

355
00:21:20,467 --> 00:21:23,636
Da-rae is having her Harvard
acceptance party. You're coming, right?

356
00:21:23,637 --> 00:21:25,555
- Honey, she got in!
- What?

357
00:21:25,556 --> 00:21:26,723
Da-rae got accepted!

358
00:21:26,724 --> 00:21:28,434
- She got in?
- Yes, look at this.

359
00:21:31,312 --> 00:21:32,645
Da-rae got accepted?

360
00:21:32,646 --> 00:21:33,814
Did they contact her?

361
00:21:34,565 --> 00:21:36,357
You didn't know?

362
00:21:36,358 --> 00:21:38,152
She got the acceptance email last night.

363
00:21:38,485 --> 00:21:40,154
I'll forward the email they sent
to the academy.

364
00:21:40,779 --> 00:21:41,989
The acceptance certificate.

365
00:21:44,658 --> 00:21:47,161
Wow, Da-rae really is amazing.

366
00:21:47,328 --> 00:21:49,204
She's really amazing.

367
00:21:49,705 --> 00:21:54,335
If Da-rae heard the news yesterday,
why didn't she say anything?

368
00:21:54,752 --> 00:21:56,962
She didn't say anything? Was she busy?

369
00:21:57,630 --> 00:22:00,674
No, Da-rae was
in her room all night.

370
00:22:02,801 --> 00:22:04,386
Then let's do
a video call with her.

371
00:22:06,305 --> 00:22:14,104
MY LOVING DAUGHTER

372
00:22:14,605 --> 00:22:16,523
- Why isn't she answering?
- She's not answering.

373
00:22:21,278 --> 00:22:22,654
She's really not answering.

374
00:22:22,655 --> 00:22:23,948
Seriously.

375
00:22:33,874 --> 00:22:35,793
I WANT TO BE ALONE

376
00:22:39,171 --> 00:22:40,797
Congratulations, guys!

377
00:22:40,798 --> 00:22:43,591
I knew you all would get accepted.

378
00:22:43,592 --> 00:22:44,677
Let's give a hand!

379
00:22:45,761 --> 00:22:47,304
- Congratulations!
- Congratulations!

380
00:22:48,973 --> 00:22:51,141
Congratulations
on the acceptance.

381
00:22:51,600 --> 00:22:53,977
Da-rae, I knew you would

382
00:22:53,978 --> 00:22:56,563
be able to do it.

383
00:22:58,649 --> 00:23:01,317
Okay, time for Da-rae and Jung-min,
to blow out the candles.

384
00:23:01,318 --> 00:23:02,236
Blow out the candles!

385
00:23:04,321 --> 00:23:05,155
Congratulations!

386
00:23:06,532 --> 00:23:08,325
- Yes!
- Congratulations!

387
00:23:08,742 --> 00:23:10,411
I'm so jealous, seriously.

388
00:23:10,661 --> 00:23:12,788
Congratulations!

389
00:23:13,622 --> 00:23:16,125
Da-rae, why aren't you
answering the phone?

390
00:23:16,500 --> 00:23:17,960
Let's have some soda.

391
00:23:19,586 --> 00:23:20,337
Are you okay?

392
00:23:21,505 --> 00:23:23,673
- Have some cake too.
- I've been wanting some.

393
00:23:23,674 --> 00:23:24,758
I'll slice it for you.

394
00:23:33,934 --> 00:23:36,270
YOU KILLED ME

395
00:23:40,107 --> 00:23:43,652
You killed me, my mother-in-law,
and the cafe owner too

396
00:23:52,161 --> 00:23:53,370
What are you thinking about?

397
00:24:01,336 --> 00:24:02,129
JUST ABOUT THE TUITION FEES
Hey.

398
00:24:02,713 --> 00:24:04,381
Your parents are property owners.

399
00:24:04,673 --> 00:24:05,758
What do you have to worry about?

400
00:24:09,511 --> 00:24:12,014
The kids are eating delivery food
over there. Want to join?

401
00:24:13,348 --> 00:24:14,266
Let's go.

402
00:24:22,983 --> 00:24:25,235
It's unfortunate for Hee-ju,
but it can't be helped.

403
00:24:25,819 --> 00:24:26,779
Right.

404
00:24:27,613 --> 00:24:29,531
Huh? What can't be helped?

405
00:24:32,201 --> 00:24:33,118
Let's take care of this.

406
00:24:37,706 --> 00:24:40,374
You coming in at night to drink

407
00:24:40,375 --> 00:24:42,586
must have been caught
on the neighborhood CCTV.

408
00:24:51,011 --> 00:24:51,970
That's right.

409
00:24:52,888 --> 00:24:55,807
I got drunk and passed out, then woke up

410
00:24:55,808 --> 00:24:56,767
and she was dead?

411
00:24:58,227 --> 00:25:00,645
I was recently mistaken
as being a kidnapper.

412
00:25:00,646 --> 00:25:02,397
I even went through interrogation.

413
00:25:03,232 --> 00:25:05,109
There really is no way out.

414
00:25:05,692 --> 00:25:07,236
Didn't you say Hwal-sung
might be the culprit?

415
00:25:08,529 --> 00:25:10,531
If we catch Min Hwal-sung,
wouldn't that solve things?

416
00:25:11,573 --> 00:25:14,618
At least we'll get to learn
what happened overnight.

417
00:25:15,035 --> 00:25:17,496
We need to find the real culprit.

418
00:25:18,288 --> 00:25:21,208
We need to at least find proof
that you didn't do this.

419
00:25:22,376 --> 00:25:25,878
And revealing the true culprit

420
00:25:25,879 --> 00:25:27,506
would be good for Hee-ju too.

421
00:25:37,975 --> 00:25:38,559
Seon.

422
00:25:40,644 --> 00:25:41,937
Thanks for believing in me.

423
00:25:42,521 --> 00:25:45,774
Let's solve this first and then talk.

424
00:25:46,817 --> 00:25:48,277
Da-rae has to go to Harvard.

425
00:25:49,069 --> 00:25:49,945
Okay.

426
00:25:52,281 --> 00:25:53,198
Well,

427
00:25:55,033 --> 00:25:56,869
I have a hiding spot,

428
00:25:57,286 --> 00:25:58,829
but the problem is how do we move her?

429
00:26:12,009 --> 00:26:12,801
What?

430
00:26:14,178 --> 00:26:15,304
Honey, take them off.

431
00:26:15,512 --> 00:26:16,762
What?

432
00:26:16,763 --> 00:26:17,973
Take off Hee-ju's clothes

433
00:26:22,603 --> 00:26:23,353
Oh.

434
00:26:26,523 --> 00:26:27,106
Key.

435
00:26:27,107 --> 00:26:28,567
Okay.

436
00:27:07,147 --> 00:27:07,856
Jeez...

437
00:27:29,336 --> 00:27:30,336
Honey, let's go.

438
00:27:30,337 --> 00:27:31,003
Okay.

439
00:27:31,004 --> 00:27:33,172
But I couldn't find Hee-ju's phone.

440
00:27:33,173 --> 00:27:34,132
It looks like someone took it.

441
00:27:34,508 --> 00:27:35,384
Let's go for now.

442
00:28:16,008 --> 00:28:17,509
But is this the right way?

443
00:28:18,760 --> 00:28:19,928
We should head home first.

444
00:28:21,471 --> 00:28:22,889
We need to be on CCTV.

445
00:28:24,599 --> 00:28:26,225
Two people get out

446
00:28:26,226 --> 00:28:27,436
and leave from behind.

447
00:28:28,478 --> 00:28:29,688
Okay, got it.

448
00:29:18,236 --> 00:29:19,112
Be careful.

449
00:29:28,997 --> 00:29:29,873
Here.

450
00:29:33,668 --> 00:29:34,669
I'll get down.

451
00:29:43,011 --> 00:29:44,262
She's heavy.

452
00:29:48,016 --> 00:29:49,518
- Get in.
- Okay.

453
00:29:58,819 --> 00:29:59,569
Let's go.

454
00:30:41,403 --> 00:30:42,737
See if anyone is coming.

455
00:30:44,030 --> 00:30:44,906
There's no one.

456
00:30:45,824 --> 00:30:46,741
Hold on.

457
00:30:51,580 --> 00:30:53,707
Wait, what should we do?
Hold on.

458
00:30:54,749 --> 00:30:56,584
- Let's move it closer.
- Closer?

459
00:30:56,585 --> 00:30:57,918
- A bit more.
- Right.

460
00:30:57,919 --> 00:30:58,962
Move her a bit closer.

461
00:30:59,838 --> 00:31:03,884
More closer.

462
00:31:04,634 --> 00:31:05,760
Just a little more.

463
00:31:07,888 --> 00:31:09,139
Is this okay?

464
00:31:23,695 --> 00:31:25,613
Honey,

465
00:31:25,614 --> 00:31:27,407
- I'm going to change the clothes first.
- Okay.

466
00:31:45,383 --> 00:31:46,717
Handcuffs.

467
00:31:46,718 --> 00:31:47,636
Prisoner uniform.

468
00:31:48,637 --> 00:31:49,637
Handcuffs?

469
00:31:49,638 --> 00:31:50,971
If you just leave him,

470
00:31:50,972 --> 00:31:52,474
your husband will go to prison.

471
00:31:53,558 --> 00:31:54,850
Make sure to carry it with you.

472
00:31:54,851 --> 00:31:58,772
Your kid will do great,
and your husband will be safe too.

473
00:32:19,251 --> 00:32:20,126
Is this good enough?

474
00:32:23,588 --> 00:32:25,047
I have no idea

475
00:32:25,048 --> 00:32:26,841
what I'm doing right now.

476
00:32:27,133 --> 00:32:29,135
I'm sorry.
I'll catch the culprit for sure.

477
00:32:31,096 --> 00:32:32,930
If you don't catch them,

478
00:32:32,931 --> 00:32:34,516
I'm going to report you.

479
00:32:34,849 --> 00:32:37,227
Okay, let's say it was a solo act.

480
00:32:37,519 --> 00:32:38,979
I won't mention that you helped me.

481
00:32:40,689 --> 00:32:42,439
What?

482
00:32:42,440 --> 00:32:44,067
Why am I an accomplice?

483
00:32:44,901 --> 00:32:46,653
I never said you were an accomplice.

484
00:32:48,905 --> 00:32:50,574
Oh, just forget it.

485
00:33:02,043 --> 00:33:03,127
Honey!

486
00:33:03,128 --> 00:33:05,213
I just got a text from Da-rae.

487
00:33:05,589 --> 00:33:08,800
Mom, I know everything about
what happened with Aunt Yi-gyeong

488
00:33:09,342 --> 00:33:10,260
What is this?

489
00:33:12,137 --> 00:33:13,597
Wait, how did she know?

490
00:33:15,640 --> 00:33:16,474
I don't know either.

491
00:33:17,392 --> 00:33:18,310
I mean,

492
00:33:18,685 --> 00:33:20,895
she won't answer
my texts or calls.

493
00:33:22,606 --> 00:33:24,398
I think I need to go see Da-rae now.

494
00:33:24,399 --> 00:33:25,482
Seon,

495
00:33:25,483 --> 00:33:27,651
you should take a taxi.
I need to deal with this car.

496
00:33:27,652 --> 00:33:29,279
- Hurry up and go.
- Okay, got it.

497
00:33:32,532 --> 00:33:33,867
Hello, is this the teacher?

498
00:33:34,159 --> 00:33:36,870
I just checked the texts.

499
00:33:38,288 --> 00:33:39,831
Where should I go?

500
00:33:45,086 --> 00:33:46,880
Jeez.

501
00:33:53,511 --> 00:33:55,930
What do you mean
you know everything?

502
00:33:56,931 --> 00:33:58,433
- Soda.
- Soda?

503
00:34:00,268 --> 00:34:02,437
Drink what's in front of you first.
Why are you drinking this?

504
00:34:03,813 --> 00:34:05,357
I KNOW WHAT YOU AND DAD DID

505
00:34:08,902 --> 00:34:09,903
Take your time eating.

506
00:34:10,570 --> 00:34:13,740
MOM

507
00:34:28,862 --> 00:34:32,256
- How many drumsticks did you eat?
- Three.

508
00:34:32,257 --> 00:34:33,125
Three?

509
00:34:33,635 --> 00:34:35,595
Look at the bone in front of you.

510
00:34:38,181 --> 00:34:39,724
Yes, here you go.

511
00:34:40,934 --> 00:34:42,935
- Thank you.
- Yes.

512
00:34:42,936 --> 00:34:44,478
- Here.
- Thank you.

513
00:34:44,479 --> 00:34:46,272
Just take one at a time.

514
00:34:46,648 --> 00:34:47,774
Here you go.

515
00:34:51,611 --> 00:34:53,196
MISSED CALL / SU-JONG

516
00:34:56,282 --> 00:34:58,450
- Okay, you all got them?
- Yes.

517
00:34:58,451 --> 00:34:59,910
Okay,

518
00:34:59,911 --> 00:35:02,371
let's all speak in a loud voice.

519
00:35:02,372 --> 00:35:03,539
Yes!

520
00:35:03,540 --> 00:35:05,374
Then, shall we practice a bit?

521
00:35:05,375 --> 00:35:06,418
Yes.

522
00:35:07,460 --> 00:35:11,588
No to forced development
and property theft!

523
00:35:11,589 --> 00:35:13,383
We oppose! We oppose!

524
00:35:13,550 --> 00:35:17,761
Stop the destruction of history!
We'll protect our buildings!

525
00:35:17,762 --> 00:35:19,597
Protect the buildings!
Protect the buildings!

526
00:35:20,056 --> 00:35:21,141
Wow, your voices
sound great today.

527
00:35:22,308 --> 00:35:23,809
Please keep it up like this.

528
00:35:23,810 --> 00:35:24,768
Yes, we will!

529
00:35:24,769 --> 00:35:26,479
- Okay, let's go!
- Let's go!

530
00:35:29,649 --> 00:35:30,858
We'll do our best.

531
00:35:30,859 --> 00:35:31,567
Put it in your pocket.

532
00:35:31,568 --> 00:35:32,192
Please contact us again.

533
00:35:32,193 --> 00:35:32,986
Sure.

534
00:35:33,987 --> 00:35:34,946
Thank you.

535
00:35:38,867 --> 00:35:40,784
Oh!
You came?

536
00:35:40,785 --> 00:35:42,287
Is it okay to film here?

537
00:35:42,996 --> 00:35:43,872
Perfect timing.

538
00:35:44,372 --> 00:35:46,331
- I'm counting on you.
- Remember what you promised.

539
00:35:46,332 --> 00:35:47,709
Got it.

540
00:35:48,168 --> 00:35:49,711
- Thanks for your support.
- Yes.

541
00:35:50,754 --> 00:35:51,420
Let's take
some shots over there.

542
00:35:51,421 --> 00:35:52,755
Okay, everyone.

543
00:35:52,756 --> 00:35:53,422
Are we all gathered?

544
00:35:53,423 --> 00:35:54,214
Oh, yes.

545
00:35:54,215 --> 00:35:55,133
Come closer, please.

546
00:35:55,633 --> 00:35:56,634
Okay, let's gather.

547
00:35:57,510 --> 00:35:59,219
Hello, everyone.

548
00:35:59,220 --> 00:36:01,138
I am Min Hwal-sung,

549
00:36:01,139 --> 00:36:03,849
the son-in-law to Pyeong-buk Gwan,

550
00:36:03,850 --> 00:36:05,393
the historic pride of Sejeong-ro.
